          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Arthur Conan Doyle</strong><br>\nArthur Conan Doyle was born on May 22, 1859, in Edinburgh, Scotland. As a young boy, he found his educational foundation at a Jesuit prep school. Doyle then pursued his university studies in medicine at the University of Edinburgh, where his proficiency in storytelling began to flourish. During his time at university, he began writing short stories, which marked the early stages of his literary career.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Beginning of Doyle's Writing Career</strong><br>\nAfter completing his medical degree, Doyle struggled to build a successful medical practice and turned to writing to fill his time. His first significant work was \"A Study in Scarlet,\" which introduced the iconic characters Sherlock Holmes and Dr. John Watson. The story was the first of its kind to combine scientific method with detective fiction and became an instant success.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Creation of Sherlock Holmes</strong><br>\nDoyle's creation, Sherlock Holmes, was inspired by one of his university professors, Dr. Joseph Bell, known for his keen observation skills. Holmes first appeared in publication in 1887 and quickly captured the fascination of readers with his brilliant deductive abilities and cold, analytical demeanor, setting the standard for future detective fiction.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
