            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 2)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Other Literary Works</strong><br>\nBesides writing detective stories, Doyle was also a prolific writer of other genres, including historical novels and science fiction. He penned \"The Lost World\" and created Professor Challenger, another character that became popular with readers. His historical novels reflected his deep interest in history and his storytelling skills in various literary forms.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Personal Beliefs and Interests</strong><br>\nDoyle was known for his strong interest in spiritualism and the occult, which grew after the deaths of several family members and close friends. He became an ardent advocate for spiritualism, writing and lecturing on the topic extensively in the later part of his life.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Doyle's Medical Career</strong><br>\nParallel to his writing, Doyle's medical background served him well. He served as a ship's surgeon and later as a military doctor during the Boer War. His experiences as a doctor influenced many of his literary works and provided material for his character's medical knowledge, especially in the Sherlock Holmes series.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
